key." Let me show you what each line does.

276
00:08:22,828 --> 00:08:24,708
The first line sends all of the Claude

277
00:08:24,808 --> 00:08:27,008
Code's request to OpenRouter, the second

278
00:08:27,088 --> 00:08:29,168
line in your key, and that's the only

279
00:08:29,228 --> 00:08:30,008
thing you change.

280
00:08:30,208 --> 00:08:31,908
Paste your key between these codes.

281
00:08:32,148 --> 00:08:34,128
The third line clears out the old

282
00:08:34,208 --> 00:08:36,448
Anthropic key so there is no chance of

283
00:08:36,508 --> 00:08:37,828
falling back to a paid key.

284
00:08:38,088 --> 00:08:40,208
And the last few lines point Claude Code's

285
00:08:40,268 --> 00:08:43,568
model slots, Opus, Sonnet, and Haiku at

286
00:08:43,768 --> 00:08:45,108
OpenRouter/free.

287
00:08:45,348 --> 00:08:47,908
OpenRouter/free is OpenRouter's free

288
00:08:47,968 --> 00:08:48,348
router.

289
00:08:48,788 --> 00:08:50,468
It picks a free model for you

290
00:08:50,528 --> 00:08:51,148
automatically.

291
00:08:51,368 --> 00:08:54,008
Then open your folder, right click, open

292
00:08:54,048 --> 00:08:56,368
the terminal, paste the block, hit Enter,

293
00:08:56,568 --> 00:08:57,428
and type Claude.

294
00:08:57,748 --> 00:08:59,768
One thing to know here is these settings

295
00:08:59,828 --> 00:09:01,908
only apply to that terminal window, so

296
00:09:01,968 --> 00:09:04,328
next time, you paste them again or you let

297
00:09:04,428 --> 00:09:06,168
Antigravity make you a shortcut.

298
00:09:06,328 --> 00:09:08,208
And this is where I almost got fooled.

299
00:09:08,388 --> 00:09:09,788
My paste failed silently.

300
00:09:10,088 --> 00:09:12,308
I typed Claude, it opened, and it looked

301
00:09:12,388 --> 00:09:12,648
fine.

302
00:09:12,848 --> 00:09:13,848
Look at the top line.

303
00:09:14,048 --> 00:09:14,868
Spot anything wrong?

304
00:09:15,188 --> 00:09:15,748
Claude Pro?

305
00:09:16,088 --> 00:09:18,148
Claude Code had quietly gone back to my

306
00:09:18,208 --> 00:09:19,028
paid subscription.

307
00:09:19,268 --> 00:09:21,388
If you see your Claude plan here, you're

308
00:09:21,448 --> 00:09:22,488
not on a free setup.

309
00:09:22,688 --> 00:09:24,828
I opened a fresh terminal, entered the

310
00:09:24,888 --> 00:09:27,268
settings one line at a time, typed Claude.

311
00:09:27,388 --> 00:09:30,508
Now it says OpenRouter/free, API usage

312
00:09:30,568 --> 00:09:30,868
billing.

313
00:09:31,128 --> 00:09:32,048
That's the free one.

314
00:09:32,288 --> 00:09:33,848
Now let's check it's really free.

315
00:09:34,028 --> 00:09:35,088
Type /model.

316
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:38,308
You'll see Opus, Sonnet, and Haiku, but

317
00:09:38,368 --> 00:09:40,568
those are just the names of the slots, not

318
00:09:40,628 --> 00:09:41,808
what's actually answering.

319
00:09:42,028 --> 00:09:44,368
I asked it, "Which model are you?" And it

320
00:09:44,408 --> 00:09:46,288
said it's a free model running through

321
00:09:46,368 --> 00:09:48,768
OpenRouter, but a model's word isn't a

322
00:09:48,828 --> 00:09:50,508
proof, so let's check the bill.

323
00:09:50,768 --> 00:09:52,828
Go to OpenRouter and open the Activity

324
00:09:52,948 --> 00:09:53,188
page.

325
00:09:53,428 --> 00:09:55,568
This is the real log of every request we

326
00:09:55,588 --> 00:09:57,708
have sent, which model answered, and what

327
00:09:57,768 --> 00:09:58,248
it costs.

328
00:09:58,468 --> 00:10:00,388
So before I scroll down, how much do you

329
00:10:00,428 --> 00:10:01,488
think this cost me?

330
00:10:01,668 --> 00:10:03,768
Three requests, about twenty-four thousand

331
00:10:03,808 --> 00:10:05,388
tokens and zero dollars.

332
00:10:05,548 --> 00:10:07,148
And one more thing that might scare you,

333
00:10:07,268 --> 00:10:09,608
if you type /usage in Claude Code, it

334
00:10:09,648 --> 00:10:11,408
might say something like thirteen cents.

335
00:10:11,608 --> 00:10:12,088
Relax.

336
00:10:12,288 --> 00:10:14,288
That's just the Claude Code estimating the

337
00:10:14,348 --> 00:10:16,248
cost at Anthropic's prices.

338
00:10:16,388 --> 00:10:18,808
The real bill is on OpenRouter, and it

339
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:19,428
says zero.

340
00:10:19,688 --> 00:10:20,968
But of course, there is a catch.

341
00:10:21,188 --> 00:10:21,848
Two, actually.

342
00:10:22,068 --> 00:10:23,108
First, limits.

343
00:10:23,368 --> 00:10:25,208
Free models are capped about fifty

344
00:10:25,248 --> 00:10:26,928
requests a day on a new account.

345
00:10:27,048 --> 00:10:29,488
Fifty sounds like plenty until you realize

346
00:10:29,568 --> 00:10:32,048
one Claude Code task can use ten or twenty

347
00:10:32,128 --> 00:10:34,408
requests because it reads files, writes

348
00:10:34,448 --> 00:10:36,828
them, checks its own work, and fixes what

349
00:10:36,868 --> 00:10:37,348
it broke.

350
00:10:37,568 --> 00:10:39,648
Hit the cap, and you'll see error four

351
00:10:39,708 --> 00:10:40,228
twenty-nine.

352
00:10:40,428 --> 00:10:42,188
Four twenty-nine is just the server

353
00:10:42,248 --> 00:10:44,368
saying, "You have used your free quota.

354
00:10:44,508 --> 00:10:46,387
Come back later." And the second is the

355
00:10:46,447 --> 00:10:46,947
privacy.

356
00:10:47,228 --> 00:10:49,528
Unlike Ollama, your prompts and your code

357
00:10:49,588 --> 00:10:52,067
now go to someone else's service, so don't

358
00:10:52,127 --> 00:10:54,568
send client code or passwords through free

359
00:10:54,628 --> 00:10:55,368
Claude models.

360
00:10:55,548 --> 00:10:56,688
Keep those on Ollama.

361
00:10:56,868 --> 00:10:58,508
So quick question before method three.

362
00:10:58,688 --> 00:11:00,588
Which one are you leaning towards so far,

363
00:11:00,848 --> 00:11:02,388
Ollama or the OpenRouter?

364
00:11:02,608 --> 00:11:04,308
Or are you waiting for the next one?

365
00:11:04,528 --> 00:11:05,488
Tell me in the comments.

366
00:11:05,688 --> 00:11:08,248
I actually read them because method three

367
00:11:08,348 --> 00:11:10,048
is where it gets really interesting.

368
00:11:10,188 --> 00:11:11,928
So here is the problem with every free

369
00:11:12,028 --> 00:11:13,388
option we have seen so far.

370
00:11:13,568 --> 00:11:15,228
Every free provider has a limit.

371
00:11:15,408 --> 00:11:16,988
Google gives you some free requests.

372
00:11:17,208 --> 00:11:18,348
NVIDIA gives you some.

373
00:11:18,568 --> 00:11:20,468
OpenRouter gives you fifty a day.

374
00:11:20,768 --> 00:11:23,488
On its own, each one runs out fast, but if

375
00:11:23,528 --> 00:11:25,728
you put them all together, that's a lot of

376
00:11:25,788 --> 00:11:26,688
free AI, right?

377
00:11:26,888 --> 00:11:29,168
And what if when one runs out, the next

378
00:11:29,248 --> 00:11:31,328
one simply takes over without you doing

379
00:11:31,388 --> 00:11:31,728
anything?

380
00:11:31,928 --> 00:11:33,888
That's exactly what OmniRoute does.

381
00:11:34,088 --> 00:11:36,128
OmniRoute is a free open source app.

382
00:11:36,328 --> 00:11:38,308
You install it on your own computer, and

383
00:11:38,388 --> 00:11:39,368
it sits in the middle.

384
00:11:39,528 --> 00:11:41,828
Claude Code talks only to OmniRoute, and

385
00:11:41,908 --> 00:11:44,208
OmniRoute decides which AI provider

386
00:11:44,308 --> 00:11:45,368
answers each request.

387
00:11:45,528 --> 00:11:47,868
So Claude Code thinks it's talking to one

388
00:11:47,968 --> 00:11:50,828
AI, but behind the scenes, OmniRoute is

389
00:11:50,888 --> 00:11:52,988
juggling many, and we install it with one

390
00:11:53,048 --> 00:11:54,768
rule, and AI does it.

391
00:11:54,988 --> 00:11:57,368
I open Antigravity and give it one prompt.

392
00:11:57,548 --> 00:11:59,628
It's in the setup kit, and it basically

393
00:11:59,708 --> 00:12:01,668
says, "Check whether Claude Code is

394
00:12:01,728 --> 00:12:03,728
installed and install it if not.

395
00:12:04,008 --> 00:12:06,568
Then install OmniRoute from GitHub, start

396
00:12:06,628 --> 00:12:08,808
it, and open the dashboard in my browser.

397
00:12:09,008 --> 00:12:11,528
And if any step fails, fix it and keep

398
00:12:11,588 --> 00:12:13,748
going." When it's done, it gives me a

399
00:12:13,808 --> 00:12:15,988
little summary table, Claude Code found,

400
00:12:16,128 --> 00:12:17,888
OmniRoute installed, server running,

401
00:12:18,048 --> 00:12:18,888
dashboard open.

402
00:12:19,128 --> 00:12:21,008
The dashboard opens in your browser at

403
00:12:21,048 --> 00:12:21,668
localhost.

404
00:12:21,848 --> 00:12:23,688
The first time, it asks for a password,

405
00:12:23,828 --> 00:12:25,488
and the default one is "change me"

406
00:12:25,588 --> 00:12:26,028
literally.

407
00:12:26,228 --> 00:12:28,768
So log in and then go straight to Settings

408
00:12:28,828 --> 00:12:30,228
and change it to something real.

409
00:12:30,428 --> 00:12:32,948
Now, the fun part here is connecting free

410
00:12:33,048 --> 00:12:33,848
AI providers.

411
00:12:33,988 --> 00:12:35,828
In the dashboard, open Providers.

412
00:12:36,128 --> 00:12:37,268
You'll see a huge list.

413
00:12:37,468 --> 00:12:39,648
For each one, you search for it, click it,

414
00:12:39,788 --> 00:12:40,528
and click Add.

415
00:12:40,708 --> 00:12:42,228
So number one is Kiro.

416
00:12:42,468 --> 00:12:45,008
Kiro is Amazon's AI coding app, and its

417
00:12:45,048 --> 00:12:47,328
free plan includes real Claude morals like

418
00:12:47,388 --> 00:12:48,148
Claude Sonnet.

419
00:12:48,368 --> 00:12:50,788
Search Kiro, click Add, and OmniRoute

420
00:12:50,848 --> 00:12:51,928
first shows a warning.

421
00:12:52,128 --> 00:12:53,928
Read it, then pick how you want to sign

422
00:12:53,988 --> 00:12:54,128
in.

423
00:12:54,308 --> 00:12:56,128
It gives you a short code and a link.

424
00:12:56,348 --> 00:12:58,188
Open the link, sign in, check that the

425
00:12:58,288 --> 00:12:59,768
code matches, and approve.

426
00:12:59,928 --> 00:13:02,088
It says device authorized, and back in

427
00:13:02,188 --> 00:13:04,248
OmniRoute, Kiro shows connected.

428
00:13:04,388 --> 00:13:06,728
And two honest things about Kiro, the free

429
00:13:06,828 --> 00:13:09,308
allowance is small, so it won't last long.

430
00:13:09,488 --> 00:13:11,528
And during sign-up, it even opened a

431
00:13:11,588 --> 00:13:13,868
subscription required page, and OmniRoute

432
00:13:13,948 --> 00:13:16,688
itself marks Kiro as terms of service

433
00:13:16,788 --> 00:13:19,088
avoid because using it this way may go

434
00:13:19,188 --> 00:13:21,588
against Kiro's rules, so this one is your

435
00:13:21,648 --> 00:13:22,848
account and your call.

436
00:13:23,028 --> 00:13:25,308
So number two is Antigravity, the same

437
00:13:25,368 --> 00:13:27,648
Google app we have been using, but this

438
00:13:27,688 --> 00:13:28,668
time as a provider.

439
00:13:28,848 --> 00:13:29,488
Click Add.

440
00:13:29,668 --> 00:13:31,168
It opens a Google sign-in.

441
00:13:31,448 --> 00:13:32,748
Pick your account and allow.

442
00:13:32,968 --> 00:13:34,908
Then your browser lands on a page that

443
00:13:34,968 --> 00:13:36,908
doesn't load, and that's normal.

444
00:13:37,068 --> 00:13:39,168
Copy the full address from the top of that

445
00:13:39,208 --> 00:13:41,328
page and paste it back into the OmniRoute

446
00:13:41,408 --> 00:13:42,168
and click Connect.

447
00:13:42,368 --> 00:13:45,008
Now you get Gemini model plus some Claude

448
00:13:45,068 --> 00:13:46,228
models within limits.

449
00:13:46,408 --> 00:13:48,188
The warning here is even stronger.

450
00:13:48,448 --> 00:13:50,668
OmniRoute says Google may restrict the

451
00:13:50,748 --> 00:13:53,108
account, so please use a spare account,

452
00:13:53,368 --> 00:13:54,368
not your main one.

453
00:13:54,568 --> 00:13:56,128
So number three is NVIDIA.

454
00:13:56,348 --> 00:13:58,808
NVIDIA, the graphics card company, also

455
00:13:58,888 --> 00:14:01,328
gives free access to bunch of AI models on

456
00:14:01,468 --> 00:14:02,948
build.nvidia.com.

457
00:14:03,088 --> 00:14:05,708
Create a free account, go to API keys, and

458
00:14:05,808 --> 00:14:07,188
click Generate API key.

459
00:14:07,408 --> 00:14:08,788
Give it a name and copy it.

460
00:14:09,008 --> 00:14:11,788
Then back in OmniRoute, open NVIDIA, click

461
00:14:11,908 --> 00:14:12,908
Add, and paste the key.

462
00:14:13,148 --> 00:14:15,408
And here, switch on Import only free

463
00:14:15,488 --> 00:14:18,008
models so only the free ones comes in, and

464
00:14:18,028 --> 00:14:18,608
then Save.

465
00:14:18,848 --> 00:14:20,228
Number four is Gemini.

466
00:14:20,512 --> 00:14:22,732
And Google AI Studio gives you a free key

467
00:14:22,772 --> 00:14:23,012
for it.

468
00:14:23,232 --> 00:14:25,832
Go to Google AI Studio, click Get API key

469
00:14:26,112 --> 00:14:28,172
and create API key and copy it.

470
00:14:28,431 --> 00:14:31,192
In OmniRoute, open Gemini, click Add and

471
00:14:31,312 --> 00:14:31,752
paste it.

472
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:34,052
Hit Check to make sure it works, and then

473
00:14:34,112 --> 00:14:34,332
Save.

474
00:14:34,592 --> 00:14:36,352
And that's four providers connected.

475
00:14:36,592 --> 00:14:38,872
Now, one by one, they are small, so let's

476
00:14:38,912 --> 00:14:40,332
make them work as one team.

477
00:14:40,572 --> 00:14:43,092
In OmniRoute, the team is called combo.

478
00:14:43,272 --> 00:14:45,532
A combo is a list of models in an order.

479
00:14:45,872 --> 00:14:48,312
The first one answers, and if it's busy,

480
00:14:48,672 --> 00:14:50,832
out of free credits, or failing, the next

481
00:14:50,912 --> 00:14:52,292
one takes over automatically.

482
00:14:52,471 --> 00:14:55,112
Go to Combos, click Create, and give it a

483
00:14:55,172 --> 00:14:55,392
name.

484
00:14:55,652 --> 00:14:57,852
I called mine Claude, and you'll see why

485
00:14:57,892 --> 00:14:59,352
that name matters in a second.

486
00:14:59,532 --> 00:15:00,532
Now, add the steps.

487
00:15:00,752 --> 00:15:03,112
For each step, you pick a provider, then a

488
00:15:03,172 --> 00:15:05,172
model, and then leave the account on

489
00:15:05,252 --> 00:15:05,792
automatic.

490
00:15:05,952 --> 00:15:06,772
Click Add Step.

491
00:15:06,992 --> 00:15:09,412
I put Gemini first, then Kairos Claude

492
00:15:09,492 --> 00:15:12,132
Sonnet, and then more free backups behind

493
00:15:12,172 --> 00:15:12,332
them.

494
00:15:12,532 --> 00:15:14,792
You can use the little up and down arrows

495
00:15:14,852 --> 00:15:15,712
to change the order.

496
00:15:15,892 --> 00:15:16,812
Top goes first.

497
00:15:16,972 --> 00:15:19,072
Then it asks for the strategy, which is

498
00:15:19,132 --> 00:15:21,632
simply how OmniRoute chooses between the

499
00:15:21,692 --> 00:15:22,952
models in your combo.

500
00:15:23,132 --> 00:15:25,631
I picked Smart Routing, so it scores each

501
00:15:25,732 --> 00:15:27,232
option and picks the best one.

502
00:15:27,452 --> 00:15:29,432
Then Save, and the combo is ready.

503
00:15:29,592 --> 00:15:32,232
Now, Claude Code needs one key to use this

504
00:15:32,332 --> 00:15:35,112
whole combo, and that's the OmniRoute API

505
00:15:35,172 --> 00:15:35,372
key.

506
00:15:35,552 --> 00:15:37,252
It's OmniRoute's own password.

507
00:15:37,472 --> 00:15:39,432
Claude Code shows this key to OmniRoute,

508
00:15:39,612 --> 00:15:42,212
and OmniRoute then uses all your provider

509
00:15:42,292 --> 00:15:43,672
keys behind the scenes.

510
00:15:43,892 --> 00:15:46,152
In the dashboard, open API Keys and click

511
00:15:46,212 --> 00:15:47,332
Create API Key.

512
00:15:47,492 --> 00:15:50,032
Give it a name, like Claude Code, and then

513
00:15:50,092 --> 00:15:50,612
create it.

514
00:15:50,832 --> 00:15:53,212
And now copy it straight away because just

515
00:15:53,272 --> 00:15:55,712
like the other keys, you only get to see

516
00:15:55,792 --> 00:15:56,292
it once.

517
00:15:56,452 --> 00:15:58,372
Now, I don't want to type commands every

518
00:15:58,412 --> 00:16:01,072
time I use this, so I give Antigravity one

519
00:16:01,132 --> 00:16:01,672
more prompt.

520
00:16:01,872 --> 00:16:04,012
It says, "Make two shortcuts on my

521
00:16:04,072 --> 00:16:04,612
desktop.

522
00:16:04,772 --> 00:16:07,012
The first is Free Claude Code," and

523
00:16:07,072 --> 00:16:08,992
launches Claude Code through OmniRoute

524
00:16:09,092 --> 00:16:09,972
using my combo.

525
00:16:10,152 --> 00:16:12,132
The second shortcut is OmniRoute

526
00:16:12,212 --> 00:16:14,372
Dashboard, which opens the control panel.

527
00:16:14,552 --> 00:16:16,992
And one important safety tip here is

528
00:16:17,072 --> 00:16:19,312
Antigravity will ask for your OmniRoute

529
00:16:19,392 --> 00:16:21,332
key while it sets this up.

530
00:16:21,412 --> 00:16:22,872
Don't paste the key into the chat.

531
00:16:23,072 --> 00:16:25,412
Ask it to open a file, paste the key into

532
00:16:25,452 --> 00:16:27,592
the file, save it, and type Continue.

533
00:16:27,752 --> 00:16:30,092
That way, your key never sits in a chat

534
00:16:30,152 --> 00:16:30,492
history.

535
00:16:30,692 --> 00:16:31,932
And then one last fix.

536
00:16:32,172 --> 00:16:34,152
When Claude Code connects to OmniRoute,

537
00:16:34,452 --> 00:16:36,732
its model menu can show every model from

538
00:16:36,772 --> 00:16:38,812
your providers, including paid ones.

539
00:16:39,012 --> 00:16:41,112
Pick a paid one by accident, and you get

540
00:16:41,192 --> 00:16:42,692
errors or, worse, a bill.

541
00:16:42,872 --> 00:16:45,072
So I give Antigravity one more prompt,

542
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:48,092
"Turn on hide paid models in OmniRoute and

543
00:16:48,152 --> 00:16:50,072
keep my Claude combo as the default."

544
00:16:50,292 --> 00:16:51,712
That's exactly what happened.

545
00:16:51,872 --> 00:16:54,012
The menu only showed free options.

546
00:16:54,192 --> 00:16:55,252
Everything's connected.

547
00:16:55,432 --> 00:16:56,452
Moment of truth.

548
00:16:56,672 --> 00:16:58,312
I double-click Free Claude Code.

